    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41716" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rhōsos</span></b> , i, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥῶσος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in
			Cilicia</i>, <i>where highly prized utensils were
			made</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 12 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rhōsĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Rhosos</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vasa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 6, 1, 13</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rhōsĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
			Rhosos</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 22, 18, § 80</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
